51x51 torus, 10% vacant, 30% minority, 100 ticks

 tolerance start   end unhappy
       0.2 0.575 0.647       5
       0.3 0.575 0.713     144
       0.4 0.575 0.867      14
       0.5 0.575 0.854      36
       0.6 0.575 0.969      10

  `start` is the same-type share after one tick, `end` after 100.
  A randomly mixed 70/30 population already sits at 0.7^2 + 0.3^2 = 0.58,
  which is what `start` measures; segregation is the rise above it.
  Asking for more similarity gets you more of it, well past what was
  asked for -- which is the whole Schelling point.
